Mesa (SiliconForest 7515336), asahi gallium: a lost context does no GPU work instead of crashing.
After a GPU fault, the G15 kernel gives the VM a sticky error: VM_BIND, GEM_CREATE and SUBMIT fail
with EIO. agx_encoder_allocate() and the batch pools then used NULL buffers, and plasmashell crashed in
agx_batch_init (2026-10-26 23:23, docs/gpu-fault-2026-10-26.md). With this patch:
- agx_device.c sets dev->lost when one of those three ioctls fails with EIO.
- agx_context_lost() (agx_state.h) marks the context lost and reports PIPE_GUILTY_CONTEXT_RESET once.
  draw_vbo, launch_grid, clear, clear_buffer, blit and resource_copy_region return at once on a lost
  context (GL robustness: commands are no-ops after a reset).
- When the loss first shows inside a new batch, the encoder and the pools use CPU scratch memory
  instead of a NULL BO; agx_batch_submit never submits a batch of a lost context.
The process still needs a new device to draw again (the VM error is per DRM file). Shaders, healthy
contexts and Vulkan are unchanged. Private SiliconForest Mesa: do not redistribute.
NOT TESTED YET. Test plan (on the M3, Mesa built into a separate prefix, not /opt/mesa-m3):
 1. Build check: ninja -C build-mesa with the patch; no new warnings in the changed files.
 2. Fault injection: tests/lost-context-inject.c (LD_PRELOAD) makes the three ioctls fail with EIO
    after LOST_AFTER_S seconds. Run es2gears_wayland, glmark2-wayland and a Qt Quick app
    (e.g. a plasmoid viewer) with LOST_AFTER_S=5 for 30 s each: before the patch they crash with
    SIGSEGV (check coredumpctl); with the patch they keep running with a frozen picture, print
    "BO creation failed" lines and exit normally when closed.
 3. Robust client: a small EGL test with EGL_EXT_create_context_robustness and
    GL_LOSE_CONTEXT_ON_RESET returns GL_GUILTY_CONTEXT_RESET from glGetGraphicsResetStatus after
    the injection.
 4. No change when healthy: tests/gpu-perf-suite.sh 60 and gles-stress, same values as without the
    patch (within run-to-run spread), 0 wrong values; llama.cpp -fa 1 text the same as the CPU.
 5. Desktop: install only after steps 1 to 4 pass, with a backup of /opt/mesa-m3.
Apply with: git -C <mesa> apply <this patch>

